From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:25:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 343/353] tools/asahi: m4-async-flip-tests: the internal
 panel's flip hold rule

Compile the production dcp_m4_int_seq() and dcp_m4_int_flight_finish()
from iomfb_m4.c against stubs and check, over random runs of
completions whose D590 says displayed or not, that the frame on screen
always stays referenced, that no frame is released twice or leaks
(after a displayed completion only that frame is held), that every
completion sends one flip event with a strictly increasing sequence,
and that the sequence counts the panel's refreshes on a jittered
120 Hz and 60 Hz grid. --mutations checks that four broken copies of
the rule are each caught.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 tools/asahi/m4-async-flip-tests.py | 244 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/asahi/run-host-tests.py      |   1 +
